# This file is a template for recording, as code, "who has to review/approve
# what." GitHub/GitLab recognize this filename automatically and add the
# relevant path's owners as PR reviewers (only takes effect once this repo
# is actually hosted on GitHub/GitLab — it isn't a git repository yet, so
# it's not enforced right now. See CONTRIBUTING.md "Scaling from individual
# -> team -> project").
#
# Keep the placeholders (@team-<service-name>) until real owners are known.
# Once people are assigned, replace these lines with actual GitHub
# usernames/teams.

# Shared libraries — changing these affects every service.
# ADR-0001 rule: a libs/ change needs an ADR + sign-off from every owner below.
/libs/netframework-core/          @team-platform
/libs/netframework-comms/         @team-platform
/libs/netframework-ai-agent/      @team-ai
/libs/netframework-contracts/     @team-platform @team-order @team-ai

# Services — each team/individual can freely change their own service's
# internals (domain/application/infrastructure/interfaces). A change that
# breaks the public contract (REST response shape, an event shape listed in
# netframework-contracts) follows the rule above instead.
/services/order-service/          @team-order
/services/ai-agent-service/       @team-ai

# Direction / rationale — changes here affect every stakeholder and get reviewed as such.
/docs/adr/                        @team-platform @team-order @team-ai
/README.md                        @team-platform
/CONTRIBUTING.md                  @team-platform
